  "rule": "A phrase decomposes into named-nerve components by stated mechanical rules (';' separates; 'territory:' prefixes, parentheticals other than the two contributory patterns, and 'A component of the B' are qualifiers on B; 'may also receive a branch from the X' and 'with contributions from the X' are contributory components; 'A and B <stem> nerves' expands to the two named nerves). A component links to FMA-sourced inventory records only on exact correspondence: R1 the name equals an un-sided record's name; R2 it equals the preferred name of an FMA class with records (all the class's records); R3 it equals an FMA-listed synonym of such a class; R4 it is the class name pluralised under {nerve->nerves, ramus->rami} (the class's records, or its level-specialisation child classes' records). A name that restricts a generic class to a region/level subset does not link to the generic record. No fuzzy matching.",
  "before_note": "Milestone 9/33 semantics (old nerve_check C8): a phrase resolved only when the full phrase string equalled a record name."
